## 10. What separates an amateur from a frame control master?

| Amateur salesperson | Frame control master |
| --- | --- |
| Tries to get everyone to like them | Focuses on building genuine trust |
| Defends every objection | Investigates the underlying concern |
| Talks to fill silence | Uses silence intentionally |
| Chases the prospect | Maintains professional boundaries |
| Lets the prospect control the entire meeting | Establishes a mutually agreed agenda |
| Reacts emotionally to rejection | Remains composed |
| Tries to convince everyone | Qualifies and disqualifies |
| Competes on price | Demonstrates differentiated value |
| Desperately asks for the sale | Helps the buyer make a clear decision |
| Memorizes scripts | Understands the psychology behind conversations |

